# Research Paper Reference URLs

## Canonical URL list

`docnav/Research/papers/github_pdf_urls.md` is the **single source of truth** for GitHub URLs to every paper PDF in this series.

When citing another paper in the series (in prose or in the References section), use the **Direct download** URL from that file:

```
https://github.com/baardev/truevalue/raw/main/docnav/Research/papers/<N>_<slug>/<N>_<slug>.pdf
```

Do **not** use `raw.githubusercontent.com` links. Paper PDFs are in Git LFS; `github.com/.../raw/main/...` resolves LFS and returns real PDF bytes. `raw.githubusercontent.com` often returns the LFS pointer text instead of the PDF.

Do **not** invent or guess URLs. Copy them from `github_pdf_urls.md` or follow its documented pattern after adding a new paper entry there.

## When to link

**Every** mention of an in-series paper number must be a hyperlink. There are no exceptions: not in the abstract, not in section headings, not in proposition labels, not in parenthetical asides, not in the References section. If the words "Paper N" or "Papers N and M" appear without a surrounding `[...](<url>)`, the file does not comply with this rule.

Link **both** citation keys and plain prose when referring to another paper in the series:

| In text | Markdown form |
|---------|----------------|
| `[Mil26a]` citation key | `[Mil26a](<direct-download-url>)` |
| `paper 3`, `Paper 3`, `papers 1 through 3` | `[paper 3](<url>)`, `[Paper 3](<url>)`, or per-number links for ranges |
| `Paper 3 of this series` | `[Paper 3 of this series](<url>)` |
| References line ending in `(Paper N of this series.)` | Include paper number in prose and append the full URL as visible plain text on the same line |
| References entry for in-series paper | Citation key plus bibliographic line plus **visible** direct-download URL (plain text, not hidden behind link anchor text) |

### References section format (required for print and plain text)

Hyperlink-only references fail in printed PDFs and text exports: anchor text such as "paper 1" prints with no URL. Every in-series References entry must therefore include the full direct-download URL as **visible plain text**. Put the URL on its own line after the bibliographic line so printed PDFs can wrap long URLs cleanly:

```
[Mil26a] Milton, J. W. *Title.* Clarity Coalition, paper 1 in this series, 2026.

<https://github.com/baardev/truevalue/raw/main/docnav/Research/papers/1_recursive-tholonic-five-constants/1_recursive-tholonic-five-constants.pdf>
```

Prose cross-references in the body may remain as `[Paper 1](<url>)` hyperlinks for digital reading. The References section is where print readers resolve what each paper number means.

**PDF build gate:** When creating a PDF, this format is mandatory. Do not run Pandoc or `research_paper_pdflatex.sh` until every in-series References entry passes. See `.cursor/rules/research-paper-pdf.mdc`.

External references (journals, books, standards) keep their normal citation format. Only **in-series** Milton / Clarity Coalition papers use URLs from `github_pdf_urls.md`.

### Quick-reference URL pattern

```
https://github.com/baardev/truevalue/raw/main/docnav/Research/papers/<N>_<slug>/<N>_<slug>.pdf
```

Copy the exact URL from `github_pdf_urls.md`; do not construct it by hand.

## Per-paper citation keys

Citation keys such as `[Mil26a]` are **not global** across the series. The same key can map to different paper numbers in different files. When linking a key, use the URL for the paper that key denotes **in that file's References section**, not a fixed global mapping.

## Adding a new paper

When a new paper is added to the series:

1. Add a `## Paper N` section to `github_pdf_urls.md` with file page and direct download URLs.
2. Use those URLs in the new paper's cross-references to prior papers.
3. After the PDF is pushed to GitHub, link citations in older papers that refer to the new paper.

After rebuilding PDFs locally: commit, `git push`, then run `./pushpng.sh` from the repo root so GitHub has the LFS objects.

## Checklist

- [ ] Every in-series `[Mil…]` / `[M26…]` citation key in the `.md` links to the correct direct-download URL
- [ ] Every plain `paper N` / `Paper N` cross-reference in prose links to the same URL
- [ ] Every in-series References entry has a visible URL on its own line (angle-bracket form)
- [ ] URLs match `docnav/Research/papers/github_pdf_urls.md` (not `raw.githubusercontent.com`)
- [ ] New papers have an entry in `github_pdf_urls.md` before cross-references are written
- [ ] PDF build blocked until References pass `.cursor/rules/research-paper-pdf.mdc` pre-build gate
